# {{app_name}} — Knowledge Vault

`knowledge/` is **first-class, committed, authored source** — the curated
memory of this project. It is the source of truth a feature points at with
the `knowledge <sector>` field; the `VOCAB-KNOWLEDGE-*` doctor rules
cross-check the field against the folders below.

> `knowledge/` is **not** `.lazuli/`. `.lazuli/` is the disposable, gitignored
> internal cache; the *derived* index built from this vault (a future
> sqlite-vec embedding store, for when `grep` stops scaling) is what lives
> there. The authored `.md` docs live **here**, in git.

This README is the canonical, in-place instantiation of the converged design
in `docs/proposals/knowledge-vault-structure.md` (lazuli repo). It is
**closed + opinionated**: the vocabulary (tiers, evidence kinds, decay
profiles) is fixed; the *set of sectors* is closed-by-default but
dev-extensible by domain.

---

## Layout

```
knowledge/<sector>/NNNN-<slug>.md
```

- `NNNN` — a zero-padded 4-digit **ordinal**. It is the migration-style join
  key: the same number threads a doc's filename, any `supersedes:` pointer,
  and `cites: { kind: item }` references. Ordering **within** a sector is by
  ordinal, not by date.
- `<slug>` — `kebab-case`, matching the doc's topic.
- `_inbox/` — the **draft staging** area (see "Gated write" below). Drafts
  land here first; they are promoted into a sector only once validated.

---

## Sectors (closed catalog, dev-extensible)

A sector is the slug in `knowledge <sector>` (grammar) **and** the folder
`knowledge/<sector>/` (file). The catalog is **closed and opinionated** —
open-vocabulary knowledge devolves into a per-project dialect, exactly what
the `.lzi` grammar forbids in the domain.

### Core sectors (the opinionated default)

| Sector       | Captures                                                                 |
|--------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `decisions`  | Why we decided: context, the options table, the choice, consequences (ADR). |
| `changes`    | A change is the lifecycle-bearing unit of work; its contents are the specs — requirement (PRD) and/or technical sketch (TECH-SPEC). Work-bearing — carries an optional `status:`. |
| `gaps`       | A framework gap: the workaround, the proposed primitive, disposition, doctor-code, wave. |
| `lazuli-way` | Doctrine / method: the governing rules, protocols, escape-hatch discipline. Typically `tier: gold`, pulled in slices. |

### Dev-extensible (domain sectors)

You **may** add sectors for **your own project's domain** (e.g. `billing`,
`iam`, `media`). The rule:

- Adding a sector = create the folder `knowledge/<sector>/` **and** reference
  it from `knowledge <sector>` on at least one feature. The two are tied by
  `VOCAB-KNOWLEDGE-SECTOR-UNKNOWN-001` (grammar ↔ file).
- A new sector inherits the **same** frontmatter schema and the **same** tier
  lifecycle. You extend the *axis* (which sectors exist), **never** the
  *internal vocabulary* (tiers, evidence kinds, decay profiles — all closed).
- Sector slugs are `kebab-case`, with **no vendor/product namespace** (mirrors
  `@plugin/<name>` ≠ core: product specifics live in `handlers/`/a plugin, not
  the vault).

---

## Frontmatter schema (the contract)

Every doc is a `.md` file opened by a `---`-fenced YAML frontmatter block.
The body below it is free markdown.

```yaml
---
# --- identity ---
title:   "Wire, not reimplementation"   # human title; matches the body H1
slug:    wire-not-reimplement           # kebab; matches the filename (minus NNNN)
sector:  lazuli-way                      # MUST match the parent folder

# --- curation / confidence (CLOSED) ---
tier:    approved                        # draft | approved | gold | deprecated
                                         #   deprecated is TERMINAL
# status: implemented                    # OPTIONAL, only on work-bearing sectors
                                         #   (e.g. changes): planned | in-progress
                                         #   | implemented | blocked. ORTHOGONAL to tier.

# --- dates (ISO yyyy-mm-dd) ---
created: 2026-05-29
updated: 2026-05-29

# --- relations (optional) ---
# supersedes: 0007-old-slug              # id of the doc this replaces; the old
                                         #   doc thereby becomes `deprecated`.

# --- evidence (optional) ---
cites:                                   # each cite carries a CLOSED EvidenceKind
  - { kind: code, ref: "customer.Customer" }   # code | url | item | issue | comment | doc
  - { kind: doc,  ref: "docs/scope-discipline.md" }

# --- facets (optional, FREE-FORM) ---
tags: [doctrine, wire]                   # free text; no global catalog

# --- decay / freshness (optional; REQUIRED when tier: gold) ---
# revalidate_by: 2027-05-29              # ISO date; a gold doc past this is STALE
# decay_profile: stable                  # stable | seasonal | volatile

# --- grading (ONLY on `evaluations` docs) ---
# score: 9.2
# threshold: 9.0
# passed: true
---
```

### Field reference

| Field           | Regime                                  | Required           |
|-----------------|-----------------------------------------|--------------------|
| `tier`          | **CLOSED** `draft\|approved\|gold\|deprecated` | yes         |
| `status`        | **CLOSED** `planned\|in-progress\|implemented\|blocked` — ORTHOGONAL to tier | only on work-bearing sectors |
| `created`/`updated` | ISO `yyyy-mm-dd`                    | yes                |
| `supersedes`    | id (`NNNN-slug` or `sector/slug`)       | no                 |
| `cites[].kind`  | **CLOSED** `code\|url\|item\|issue\|comment\|doc` | no       |
| `tags`          | **FREE-FORM** (no enum)                 | no                 |
| `revalidate_by` | ISO date                                | yes if `gold`      |
| `decay_profile` | **CLOSED** `stable\|seasonal\|volatile` | no                 |
| `score`/`threshold`/`passed` | numeric / bool             | only on `evaluations` |

> **No `source` field.** Provenance (`human`/`ai`/`imported`) was dropped: in
> an AI-curated harness it is near-constant. `tier` carries the trust signal.

---

## Tier vs. status (orthogonal axes)

- **`tier`** is *knowledge confidence* — how much to trust this doc.
- **`status`** is *work progress* — only meaningful on work-bearing sectors
  (`changes`, and any domain sector that tracks delivery). It is **orthogonal**:
  a change can be `tier: approved` (reviewed, trusted) while `status:
  in-progress` (not yet shipped).

`deprecated` is the **terminal** tier — there is no path back out of it.

---

## Deprecation is DERIVED, never a manual move

You do **not** scan-and-move stale docs. When a new doc replaces an old one,
the new doc declares `supersedes: <old-id>` at write-time, and the old doc's
tier becomes `deprecated`. There is **no `archive/` tree** — "obsolete" is a
tier, not a directory position. This keeps `git log --follow` intact:

- **Append-only history, dated/signed** = `git` (history size ≠ context size).
- **Current curated state** = the working tree (the "gold projection" the
  agent reads — the pile is in git, the projection is on disk).

---

## Gated write (the anti-`lixão` gate)

Memory writes are **not free**. The #1 failure of agent memory is the dump: a
giant folder of unvalidated, stale, redundant notes the agent drowns in. The
cure is migration discipline — drafts stage in `_inbox/`, and are promoted
into a sector only when they pass **four gates**, each enforced by a
`VOCAB-KNOWLEDGE-*` rule:

| Discipline            | What it means                                                        | Enforcing rule                          |
|-----------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
| **In-catalog**        | a doc only exists under a `<sector>/` referenced by `knowledge <sector>` | `VOCAB-KNOWLEDGE-SECTOR-UNKNOWN-001` |
| **Earned promotion**  | nothing is born `gold`; it must have passed through `draft` in git   | `VOCAB-KNOWLEDGE-UNGATED-WRITE-001`     |
| **Durable**           | a `gold` doc past its `revalidate_by` goes stale and leaves the projection | `VOCAB-KNOWLEDGE-STALE-001`        |
| **Cited / resolvable**| `cites:` cannot point at a symbol the compiler doesn't know          | `VOCAB-KNOWLEDGE-DANGLING-CITE-001`     |
| **Non-redundant**     | one truth per topic: two `gold` docs on a topic need a `supersedes`  | `VOCAB-KNOWLEDGE-DUP-TOPIC-001`         |

Promotion flow: author in `_inbox/` as `tier: draft` → review → move to
`knowledge/<sector>/NNNN-<slug>.md` and bump `tier:` to `approved`/`gold`.
Because the gate keys on **git history**, a `gold` doc that never had a draft
commit fires `UNGATED-WRITE` — land it as `draft` first.

---

## Retrieval (the north star)

How the agent pulls knowledge back out:

- **By sector** — the directory (`knowledge/decisions/`).
- **By tag** — a frontmatter scan (`tags: [...]`, AND-containment).
- **By context pack** — the future `context <name>` keyword (NOT `pack`,
  which the registry owns): a named query over sectors + tags + tier, on two
  axes — *purpose* (durable, e.g. `onboarding`) and *handoff* (run-memory
  recency, ordered by `updated`).

When `grep` stops scaling, the derived index (sqlite-vec) is generated from
this vault into `.lazuli/` — never the other way around.
